/-!
# The Noetherian spreadout step

Let `A` be a local ring, `B` an `A`-algebra of finite presentation and `N` a finitely presented
`B`-module. This file proves that there is a *finitely generated* ideal `I ⊆ 𝔪_A` such that
`(A ⧸ I) ⊗_A N` is a **free** `A ⧸ I`-module.

This is the Noetherian approximation step in the proof of Stacks Tag 0AT8, and it is the only
step of that proof which is not formal: it is what produces the ideal `I` and the projectivity
of the spreadout module over the base.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Flatness.free_tensorProduct_of_eq_comap_maximalIdeal` is the ring-theoretic core,
  stated for the contraction of `𝔪_A` to an arbitrary subring: over a local ring `A` with
  subring `R₀` and `𝔭₀ = 𝔪_A ∩ R₀`, every `R₀`-module becomes free after base change along
  `R₀ → A ⧸ 𝔭₀ A`.
* `Stacks.Flatness.exists_fg_ideal_le_maximalIdeal_free_tensorProduct` is the spreadout step
  itself.

## Implementation notes

The source of Tag 0AT8 chooses "a local subring `A₀ ⊆ A` essentially of finite type over `ℤ`, a
finite type ring map `A₀ → B₀` with `B = A ⊗_{A₀} B₀`, and a finite `B₀`-module `N'₀` with
`N' = B ⊗_{B₀} N'₀`", and then claims that `I = 𝔪_{A₀} A` works. **No such localized subring
has to be produced.** Stacks 00R1, proved as
`Algebra.exists_subring_finiteType_int_isPushout_isBaseChange`, already yields a subring
`R₀ ⊆ A` of finite type over `ℤ` with `B = A ⊗_{R₀} S₀` and `N = B ⊗_{S₀} M₀`, and the ideal
`I = 𝔭₀ A` generated by the contraction `𝔭₀ = 𝔪_A ∩ R₀` does the same job. It is finitely
generated because `R₀` is Noetherian, and contained in `𝔪_A` by construction.

The localization of `R₀` at `𝔭₀` is only needed to see that `A ⧸ I` is an algebra over the
*residue field* `κ(𝔭₀)`. That is obtained here instead from
`IsFractionRing (R₀ ⧸ 𝔭₀) 𝔭₀.ResidueField` by `IsLocalization.lift`: every element of
`R₀ ∖ 𝔭₀` avoids `𝔪_A` and is therefore already a unit in `A`.

The two base-change cancellations are Mathlib's, used in the two directions that the towers
`R₀ → A → B` and `R₀ → κ(𝔭₀) → A ⧸ I` call for: `Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange` turns
`B ⊗_{S₀} M₀` into `A ⊗_{R₀} M₀`, which is the identity `N = M_λ ⊗_{R_λ} R` that Stacks 00R1's
statement leaves implicit, and `TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange` moves
`(A ⧸ I) ⊗_{R₀} M₀` across `κ(𝔭₀)`.

Neither statement needs `A` to be Noetherian, and the module is not required to be flat. The
module universes are free: only `A` and `B` are required to share a universe, which is what
Stacks 00R1 imposes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AT8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AT8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00R1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00R1)
-/

@[expose] public section

open TensorProduct

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.Flatness

/-- An algebra of finite presentation over `A` is small relative to the universe of `A`: it is
a quotient of a polynomial ring in finitely many variables over `A`. -/
public theorem small_of_algebra_finitePresentation (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : Type v)
    [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra.FinitePresentation A B] : Small.{u} B := by
  obtain ⟨n, f, hf⟩ :=
    (Algebra.FiniteType.iff_quotient_mvPolynomial'' (R := A) (S := B)).mp inferInstance
  exact small_of_surjective (f := f) hf

/-- Over a local ring `A`, let `R₀ ⊆ A` be a subring and `𝔭₀` the contraction of `𝔪_A` to it.
Then every `R₀`-module becomes free after base change along `R₀ → A ⧸ 𝔭₀ A`.

The reason is that `A ⧸ 𝔭₀ A` is an algebra over the residue field `κ(𝔭₀)`: the map
`R₀ → A ⧸ 𝔭₀ A` kills `𝔭₀`, and every element of `R₀` outside `𝔭₀` avoids `𝔪_A`, hence is a
unit in `A` and a fortiori in the quotient, so `IsLocalization.lift` extends the map along
`IsFractionRing (R₀ ⧸ 𝔭₀) κ(𝔭₀)`. Base change through a field produces a free module, and
cancelling `κ(𝔭₀)` identifies it with the base change through `R₀`.

This is the mechanism behind
`Stacks.Flatness.exists_fg_ideal_le_maximalIdeal_free_tensorProduct`; no finiteness of the
module is needed here, and `R₀` need not be Noetherian. -/
public theorem free_tensorProduct_of_eq_comap_maximalIdeal {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsLocalRing A] (R₀ : Subring A) (p₀ : Ideal R₀) [p₀.IsPrime]
    (hp₀ : p₀ = (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).comap (algebraMap R₀ A))
    (M₀ : Type v) [AddCommGroup M₀] [Module R₀ M₀] :
    Module.Free (A ⧸ p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A))
      ((A ⧸ p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A)) ⊗[R₀] M₀) := by
  set I : Ideal A := p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A)
  have hmem : ∀ a : R₀, a ∈ p₀ → (algebraMap R₀ (A ⧸ I)) a = 0 := by
    intro a ha
    show Ideal.Quotient.mk I ((algebraMap R₀ A) a) = 0
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
  have : IsDomain (R₀ ⧸ p₀) := Ideal.Quotient.isDomain p₀
  let g : (R₀ ⧸ p₀) →+* (A ⧸ I) := Ideal.Quotient.lift p₀ (algebraMap R₀ (A ⧸ I)) hmem
  have hunit : ∀ y : nonZeroDivisors (R₀ ⧸ p₀), IsUnit (g y) := by
    rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
    have hane : a ∉ p₀ := fun h ↦
      (nonZeroDivisors.coe_ne_zero ⟨_, hy⟩) (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 h)
    have hnm : (algebraMap R₀ A) a ∉ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A := fun h ↦ hane (hp₀ ▸ h)
    exact (IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.1 hnm).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
  let _ialg : Algebra p₀.ResidueField (A ⧸ I) :=
    (IsLocalization.lift (M := nonZeroDivisors (R₀ ⧸ p₀)) hunit).toAlgebra
  have _tow : IsScalarTower R₀ p₀.ResidueField (A ⧸ I) := by
    refine IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (RingHom.ext fun r ↦ ?_)
    show (algebraMap R₀ (A ⧸ I)) r = _
    rw [RingHom.comp_apply, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R₀ (R₀ ⧸ p₀) p₀.ResidueField r]
    show _ = IsLocalization.lift hunit _
    rw [IsLocalization.lift_eq]
    rfl
  exact Module.Free.of_equiv
    (AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R₀ p₀.ResidueField (A ⧸ I) (A ⧸ I) M₀)

/-- If `N` is a module over `B` and over two rings `X`, `Y` mapping compatibly to `B`, with
`X`-scalars and `Y`-scalars on `N` factoring through `B`, then `X`, `Y` act compatibly on `N`. -/
private theorem isScalarTower_of_isScalarTower_algebra {X Y N : Type*} (B : Type*) [CommSemiring X]
    [CommSemiring Y] [CommSemiring B] [Algebra X Y] [Algebra X B] [Algebra Y B]
    [IsScalarTower X Y B] [AddCommMonoid N] [Module X N] [Module Y N] [Module B N]
    [IsScalarTower X B N] [IsScalarTower Y B N] : IsScalarTower X Y N :=
  ⟨fun x y n ↦ by
    rw [← algebraMap_smul B (x • y) n, ← algebraMap_smul B y n,
      Algebra.smul_def x y, map_mul, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply, mul_smul, algebraMap_smul]⟩

/-- **The Noetherian spreadout step of Stacks Project, Tag 0AT8.** Let `A` be a local ring, `B`
an `A`-algebra of finite presentation and `N` a finitely presented `B`-module. Then there is a
finitely generated ideal `I` of `A`, contained in the maximal ideal, such that `(A ⧸ I) ⊗_A N`
is a *free* `A ⧸ I`-module.

Tag 0AT8 uses exactly this to produce its pure spreadout: the spreadout module of the
base-changed situation is `N' ⧸ I N'`, whose projectivity over `A ⧸ I` is this freeness, and
whose localization map is then universally injective by Tag 05FR.

See the module docstring for why no localized subring of `A` has to be constructed, and for the
two base-change cancellations the proof uses. -/
public theorem exists_fg_ideal_le_maximalIdeal_free_tensorProduct {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [IsLocalRing A] (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra.FinitePresentation A B]
    (N : Type v) [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]
    [Module.FinitePresentation B N] :
    ∃ I : Ideal A, I.FG ∧ I ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ∧
      Module.Free (A ⧸ I) ((A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] N) := by
  obtain ⟨R₀, S₀, M₀, cS₀, aR₀S₀, aS₀B, tR₀S₀B, agM₀, mS₀M₀, mS₀N, tS₀BN, f,
    hZ, hS₀, hM₀, hpush, hbc⟩ :=
    Algebra.exists_subring_finiteType_int_isPushout_isBaseChange (R := A) (S := B) N
  let _i1 : Module R₀ M₀ := Module.compHom M₀ (algebraMap R₀ S₀)
  have _t1 : IsScalarTower R₀ S₀ M₀ := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  have _t2 : IsScalarTower R₀ A B := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  let _i2 : Module R₀ N := Module.compHom N (algebraMap R₀ A)
  have _t3 : IsScalarTower R₀ A N := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  have _t4 : IsScalarTower R₀ B N := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun r n ↦ by
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R₀ A B, algebraMap_smul, algebraMap_smul]
  have _t5 : IsScalarTower R₀ S₀ N := isScalarTower_of_isScalarTower_algebra B
  have _n0 : IsNoetherianRing R₀ := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing ℤ _
  have hN : IsBaseChange A (f.restrictScalars R₀) :=
    IsBaseChange.of_equiv
      ((Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange R₀ A S₀ B M₀).symm.trans
        (hbc.equiv.restrictScalars A)) (fun x ↦ by simp)
  set p₀ : Ideal R₀ := (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).comap (algebraMap R₀ A)
  have _hpp : p₀.IsPrime := Ideal.IsPrime.comap _
  refine ⟨p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A), Ideal.FG.map (IsNoetherian.noetherian _) _,
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr le_rfl, ?_⟩
  have hfree := free_tensorProduct_of_eq_comap_maximalIdeal R₀ p₀ rfl M₀
  exact Module.Free.of_equiv
    ((AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R₀ A
        (A ⧸ p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A)) (A ⧸ p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A)) M₀).symm.trans
      (AlgebraTensorModule.congr
        (LinearEquiv.refl (A ⧸ p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A)) (A ⧸ p₀.map (algebraMap R₀ A)))
        hN.equiv))

/-- **The Noetherian spreadout step of Stacks Project, Tag 0AT8, in arbitrary universes.**
Let `A` be a local ring, `B` an `A`-algebra of finite presentation and `N` a finitely presented
`B`-module. Then there is a finitely generated ideal `I` of `A`, contained in the maximal
ideal, such that `(A ⧸ I) ⊗_A N` is a *free* `A ⧸ I`-module.

This is `Stacks.Flatness.exists_fg_ideal_le_maximalIdeal_free_tensorProduct` with the universe
of `B` freed. Tag 0AT8 needs this form: there the base ring is a local ring of `A`, while the
algebra is a base change of `B` and therefore lives in the join of the two universes.

The reduction replaces `B` by the model `MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ ker f` supplied by finite
presentation itself, which lives in the universe of `A`. Nothing has to be transported back,
because the conclusion does not mention `B`; the only transport needed is
`Module.FinitePresentation` of `N` along the isomorphism, and that is
`Module.FinitePresentation.trans` applied to a ring isomorphism.

`Shrink.{u} B` is the other obvious model — `Stacks.Flatness.small_of_algebra_finitePresentation`
supplies the required smallness — but it is the wrong one here: `Shrink` transports an `SMul A`
instance from `B`, which collides with the `Algebra A (Shrink B)` the argument has to install,
and the resulting diamond is not definitional. The polynomial-quotient model carries only its
canonical instances. -/
public theorem exists_fg_ideal_le_maximalIdeal_free_tensorProduct_of_universe
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] (B : Type v) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [Algebra.FinitePresentation A B]
    (N : Type w) [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]
    [Module.FinitePresentation B N] :
    ∃ I : Ideal A, I.FG ∧ I ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ∧
      Module.Free (A ⧸ I) ((A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] N) := by
  obtain ⟨n, f, hfs, -⟩ := Algebra.FinitePresentation.out (R := A) (A := B)
  set B₀ := MvPolynomial (Fin n) A ⧸ RingHom.ker f.toRingHom
  let eq : B₀ ≃ₐ[A] B := Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hfs
  let _algB₀B : Algebra B₀ B := (eq : B₀ →+* B).toAlgebra
  have _towAB₀B : IsScalarTower A B₀ B :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (RingHom.ext fun a ↦ (eq.commutes a).symm)
  have _fpAB₀ : Algebra.FinitePresentation A B₀ := Algebra.FinitePresentation.equiv eq.symm
  let _modB₀N : Module B₀ N := Module.compHom N (algebraMap B₀ B)
  have _towB₀BN : IsScalarTower B₀ B N := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  have _towAB₀N : IsScalarTower A B₀ N := isScalarTower_of_isScalarTower_algebra B
  have hsmul : ∀ b x : B₀, eq (b • x) = b • eq x := by
    intro b x
    rw [Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, map_mul]
    rfl
  let eL : B₀ ≃ₗ[B₀] B := { eq.toRingEquiv with map_smul' := hsmul }
  have _fpB₀B : Module.FinitePresentation B₀ B := Module.FinitePresentation.of_equiv eL
  have _fpB₀N : Module.FinitePresentation B₀ N := Module.FinitePresentation.trans B₀ N B
  exact exists_fg_ideal_le_maximalIdeal_free_tensorProduct B₀ N

end Stacks.Flatness

end
